  "slug": "genome-evolution-3106",
  "summary": "Long-read and Hi-C assemblies now reach chromosome scale in durum wheat and extend to sugarcane GWAS in polyploids.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is the construction of contiguous reference genomes for polyploid and non-model eukaryotes from long-read and proximity-ligation data. Two preprints report chromosome-scale assemblies of durum wheat landraces Chili and Mahmoudi from HiFi and Hi-C reads, each resolved into 14 pseudomolecules. A third preprint presents a PacBio HiFi draft of Greyia radlkoferi, a 206 Mb assembly with scaffold N50 of 10.1 Mb and 17,804 predicted protein-coding genes, at draft rather than chromosome-scale resolution. The published study on sugarcane extends this logic into functional genetics: a phased POJ2878 genome built with Pore-C is paired with polyploid-tailored GWAS across 981 accessions linking loci to sucrose storage. What is new is the combination of phased assembly with association analysis in a polyploid crop, rather than assembly alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-05-31"
}
